Subject: [PATCH] test: a small test kit, byte-identical helpers adopted, the
 no-db guard, TZ pinned, a values golden; the request-kind table (setup and
 new files)

The kit (v0.43 R3.1, R3.2, R3.5): src/utils/test-utils.ts for jsdom suites (respond, responding,
advance, posts, sent, rollServer, minutesAgo, brokenImages, normalizeIds, normalizeTimes,
atFixedTime, markup, ordered) with its own table test; src/utils/test-utils-node.ts for node
suites (prismaMock, prismaFake, resetPrisma, guardNoDb, routeCall); src/mocks/dice-renderer.ts
(NO_DICE_RENDERER); and SheetProviders in src/mocks/sheet-providers/, the sheet's contexts as
CharacterPane makes them, for the goldens. Nothing outside tests imports any of it.

Adopted (R3.3, setup lines only): 41 byte-identical local helpers replaced by kit imports, under
their old local names where they differ (respond 15, responding 3, advance 11, posts 3, ago 5,
brokenBeforeMount 4); the 18 identical 3d-dice-react factories by the dice-renderer requireActual;
the 33 relative jest.setup imports of prismaMock by @/utils/test-utils-node. guardNoDb() after the
imports of the 25 route suites that mock every db module (R3.4). jest.config.ts pins TZ=UTC for
every worker; unicorn/filename-case ignores __snapshots__/. C9 (values.golden.test.ts, retired
with C1 in commit 26): every constant of src/constants, the exported timings tests read, and every
src/mocks fixture, keyed by name. W-a's part: src/constants/roll-kinds.ts and its test, and
RollKindInfo appended to src/types/roll.ts (R1.6, new files only; no reader changed yet).

L1 in the builder's worktree (R/tools/l1.sh, 2026-11-03 06:13-06:19 UTC): jest 293 suites, 8,954
tests (base 290 and 8,607, every base test passed with at least its asserts; 347 new: the kit's 44,
C9's 281, roll-kinds' 22), 0 red; typegen and tsc clean; eslint 0 errors, 999 warnings (the base's,
gate 9 equal); gates 1, 2-12 ok, gate 8 on the 25 guarded suites. Gate 1b differs only on the 18
replaced 3d-dice-react factories, its planned allowlist rows; the three `responding` adoptions
are noted for review (the kit wraps respond() where the copies wrote the object out: the same
three fields, resolved).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
